<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>dev.verastack.rigseed</id>

  <name>rigseed</name>
  <summary>A desktop client for qBittorrent</summary>

  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>Apache-2.0</project_license>

  <developer id="dev.verastack">
    <name>Verastack Labs</name>
  </developer>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">rigseed.desktop</launchable>

  <description>
    <p>
      rigseed is a desktop interface for qBittorrent. It bundles qbittorrent-nox,
      the headless daemon, and starts it itself, so there is nothing to install or
      configure first. It speaks the same Web API that an existing qBittorrent
      exposes, so it can also attach to one you already run, on this machine or
      on another.
    </p>
    <p>What it gives you:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>A transfer list with status, category and tag filters, a live speed graph, and three densities</li>
      <li>An Easy view in plain language, stating four minutes left rather than a rate and an ETA you combine yourself</li>
      <li>Eight accents across a light and a dark mode, retinting every surface live with nothing to restart</li>
      <li>A first launch that asks where files go, how fast to go and what to seed, each beside the sentence saying what it does</li>
    </ul>
  </description>

  <url type="homepage">https://rigseed.verastack.dev/</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/verastack-labs/rigseed-app/issues</url>
  <url type="vcs-browser">https://github.com/verastack-labs/rigseed-app</url>

